  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In a June 4, 2025 FTC transcript, Chris Mufarrige said AI would change valued skills and criticized AI-animated art as contrary to attentive engagement. He described chatbot deception and sycophancy as problems and advocated non-expert watermarking so people know they are dealing with an inhuman presentation. He argued that AI is not truly intelligence but a calculative machine, and said leaving such tools with children risks inhuman effects and less human development. In an undated reported statement, he said condemning a technology merely because it could be used problematically is inconsistent with the law and ordered liberty.",
   "sids": [
    "s2",
    "s3",
    "s4",
    "s5",
    "s6",
    "s7",
    "s1"
   ],
